1. I need to extend `c_mkdir.c` to support the `-m` / `--mode` option in addition to the existing `-p` / `--parents` support.

Key requirements:
1. Accept `-m MODE`, `-mMODE`, `--mode MODE` and `--mode=MODE`
2. Last mode wins
3. Reject invalid or empty mode arguments before creating operands, with "invalid mode" on stderr and status 1
4. An empty whole argument is distinct from a valid empty symbolic assignment such as `o=`
5. Numeric modes are octal (base eight), 0000..7777
6. Symbolic modes use GNU Coreutils 9.11 directory semantics with `a=rwx` as the point of departure
7. Accept u/g/o/a selectors, +, -, = operators, rwxXst permissions and permission-copy u/g/o
8. Comma-separated clauses, successive operations evaluated in order
9. `+` adds, `-` removes, `=` replaces selected permissions
10. Permission copying copies source class's ordinary rwx bits to selected classes
11. Conditional X supplies search for directories
12. Empty assignments clear selected ordinary permissions
13. With explicit who (including a), changes are independent of umask
14. With omitted who, +/- affect only bits not protected by umask; = replaces with requested bits filtered by umask
15. Preserve GNU special-bit semantics for directory set-ID bits
16. Numeric modes of 4 or fewer octal digits preserve unspecified directory set-ID bits; 5+ digits explicitly clear unspecified set-ID bits
17. s addresses set-user-ID for u, set-group-ID for g; t addresses sticky for o (including a or omitted who)
18. With parents enabled, explicit modes apply only to newly created final directories
19. Newly created intermediate parents retain 0777 masked by umask with owner write and search ensured
20. Existing directories retain all permissions; -m does not chmod existing final directories accepted by -p

